unction"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. Here's what happened:\n\n1. **Service resolution**: `payments` wasn't a valid service ID; the actual service is **`payments-api`** (resolved by probing the registry).\n\n2. **Rollback**: `payments-api` v5.1.0 (deployed this morning) was unhealthy with an **18% error rate** across all regions. Deployment history showed **v5.0.0 was the last healthy release**, so I rolled back to it. This is a known-good version, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n\n3. **Verified recovery**: All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v5.0.0 and the service is **healthy with a 0.2% error rate**.\n\n4. **Incident**: Opened **SEV2 incident INC-0001**, paged on-call, with a summary of the v5.1.0 regression and the successful rollback.\n\nOne note: v5.1.0's only history entry is \"degraded\" \u2014 so if the team re-releases a fixed v5.1.1, it will be the first time that version runs healthy in production and would require change-manager approval per policy.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}